{
  "schema": "loadsketch/design@1",
  "name": "Slack style: metastable failure after the cache was emptied (2022-02-22)",
  "description": "Sending a message in Slack goes through the Webapp → a Vitess write, then Admin Server → Channel Server → Gateway Server, which pushes it to the websocket; slow work goes Kafkagate → Kafka → JQRelay → Redis to the job workers. Reads (including the boot query of a starting client) check Mcrouter/Memcached first and Vitess only on a miss. On 2022-02-22 a rolling Consul upgrade at peak restarted the Consul agent on 25% of the machines; cache nodes were replaced by empty ones, the hit ratio fell and the boot queries all hit Vitess. The overloaded database timed out more, the cache could not fill again, and client retries added load. After the trigger was gone the system still did not recover, until boot requests were rate limited. Sources: https://slack.engineering/slacks-incident-on-2-22-22/ , https://slack.engineering/real-time-messaging/ , https://slack.engineering/scaling-slacks-job-queue/ . The parameters are scaled down for teaching; they are not Slack's real numbers.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "active",
      "kind": "client",
      "label": "Started clients (send and read messages)",
      "pos": [0, 120],
      "params": { "weight": 3, "priority": "normal" }
    },
    {
      "id": "boot",
      "kind": "client",
      "label": "Starting clients (boot query)",
      "pos": [0, 360],
      "params": { "weight": 1, "priority": "batch" }
    },
    {
      "id": "envoy",
      "kind": "load_balancer",
      "label": "Envoy (edge LB)",
      "pos": [270, 240],
      "params": { "policy": "p2c" }
    },
    {
      "id": "bootlimit",
      "kind": "rate_limiter",
      "label": "Boot rate limit (added during the incident)",
      "pos": [540, 240],
      "params": { "limit": "rate", "ratePerSec": 100000, "burst": 100000, "appliesTo": "batch" }
    },
    {
      "id": "webapp",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Webapp (Hack monolith)",
      "pos": [810, 240],
      "params": {
        "instances": 12,
        "concurrency": 32,
        "serviceMs": { "mean": 6, "cv": 1 },
        "queueLimit": 200
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "mcrouter",
      "kind": "cache",
      "label": "Mcrouter + Memcached",
      "pos": [1080, 60],
      "params": {
        "mode": "lru",
        "capacityKeys": 120000,
        "ttlS": 0,
        "stampede": "none",
        "instances": 4,
        "concurrency": 16,
        "opMs": { "mean": 0.3, "cv": 0.5 }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "vitess",
      "kind": "sharded_db",
      "label": "Vitess + MySQL (sharded)",
      "pos": [1080, 240],
      "params": {
        "shards": 4,
        "replicas": 1,
        "readFrom": "any",
        "connections": 6,
        "readMs": { "mean": 8, "cv": 1 },
        "writeMs": { "mean": 10, "cv": 1 },
        "queueLimit": 3000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "admin",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Admin Server (finds the channel's CS)",
      "pos": [1080, 420],
      "params": { "instances": 4, "concurrency": 64, "serviceMs": { "mean": 1, "cv": 0.5 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "channel",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Channel Server (stateful, fan-out)",
      "pos": [1350, 420],
      "params": { "instances": 4, "concurrency": 64, "serviceMs": { "mean": 2, "cv": 1 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "gateway",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Gateway Server (websocket push)",
      "pos": [1620, 420],
      "params": { "instances": 6, "concurrency": 128, "serviceMs": { "mean": 2, "cv": 1 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "kafkagate",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Kafkagate (job entry)",
      "pos": [1080, 600],
      "params": { "instances": 2, "concurrency": 64, "serviceMs": { "mean": 1, "cv": 0.5 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "kafka",
      "kind": "queue",
      "label": "Kafka (job topic)",
      "pos": [1350, 600],
      "params": { "delivery": "at_least_once", "visibilityTimeoutMs": 60000, "maxReceives": 5 }
    },
    {
      "id": "jqrelay",
      "kind": "worker",
      "label": "JQRelay (Kafka → Redis)",
      "pos": [1620, 600],
      "params": { "instances": 2, "concurrency": 16, "serviceMs": { "mean": 2, "cv": 0.5 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "redisq",
      "kind": "queue",
      "label": "Redis job queue",
      "pos": [1080, 780],
      "params": { "delivery": "at_least_once", "visibilityTimeoutMs": 60000, "maxReceives": 3 }
    },
    {
      "id": "jobs",
      "kind": "worker",
      "label": "Job workers (push, indexing, billing)",
      "pos": [1350, 780],
      "params": { "instances": 16, "concurrency": 12, "serviceMs": { "mean": 30, "cv": 1 } }
    },
    {
      "id": "push",
      "kind": "service",
      "label": "Mobile push (external)",
      "pos": [1620, 780],
      "params": { "instances": 2, "concurrency": 128, "serviceMs": { "mean": 60, "cv": 0.8 } }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    { "from": "active", "to": "envoy", "retries": 2, "backoffMs": 200 },
    { "from": "boot", "to": "envoy", "retries": 3, "backoffMs": 200 },
    { "from": "envoy", "to": "bootlimit" },
    { "from": "bootlimit", "to": "webapp" },
    { "from": "webapp", "to": "mcrouter" },
    { "from": "webapp", "to": "vitess", "timeoutMs": 500, "retries": 1, "backoffMs": 50 },
    { "from": "webapp", "to": "admin", "on": "write", "timeoutMs": 300 },
    { "from": "webapp", "to": "kafkagate", "on": "write", "timeoutMs": 300 },
    { "from": "admin", "to": "channel" },
    { "from": "channel", "to": "gateway" },
    { "from": "kafkagate", "to": "kafka" },
    { "from": "kafka", "to": "jqrelay" },
    { "from": "jqrelay", "to": "redisq" },
    { "from": "redisq", "to": "jobs" },
    { "from": "jobs", "to": "push", "timeoutMs": 2000 }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "n1",
      "text": "Try this: 1) Run the scenario: at second 45 half of the cache nodes are replaced by empty ones and come back 10 seconds later, cold. Watch the Vitess queue, and the webapp rejecting requests when its queue is full; after the trigger is gone, errors drag on for about a minute (seconds 70–140: about 0.5% errors, p99 about 840 ms; without the event 0% and about 100 ms). 2) Set the per-second limit of \"Boot rate limit\" to 300: the errors of started clients go away, at the cost of blocked boot requests (429). 3) Set the cache's stampede protection to lease, or give webapp→vitess a retry budget of 0.1, and compare how fast it recovers.",
      "pos": [270, 760],
      "width": 520
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "text": "Simplified: the real boot query is a scatter query (it hits every shard). The simulator has no scatter-gather, so a plain read stands in for it. There are no parts for the Gateway Server's websocket connections or the Channel Server's consistent-hash ring either.",
      "pos": [900, 760],
      "width": 520
    }
  ]
}
